* OFTPPRM0 - OFTPD monitor settings
*
* KEYWORD=VALUE, blanks or commas between them, '*' in column 1
* starts a comment. Columns 73-80 are ignored.
*
* ODETTEID     this installation's Odette ID (required)
* PORT         OFTP port for calls from partners          (3305)
* INPREFIX     received files are INPREFIX.<virtual name>  (OFTP.IN)
* TMPPREFIX    files while being received                  (OFTP.TMP)
* MAXSESS      sessions at a time                          (4)
* SDEB         exchange buffer, 128..8192                  (4096)
* CREDIT       buffers before a credit, 1..999             (99)
* TIMEOUT      seconds to wait for the partner             (60)
* RETRY        seconds before a send is retried: RETRY times
*              the attempts so far, at most a day           (300)
* MAXRETRY     attempts per send, 0 = no limit; then our own
*              file is held, a relayed one given up (NERP)  (10)
* TLRECL       LRECL of received text files (VB)           (255)
* UBLKSIZE     BLKSIZE of received unstructured files (U)  (6144)
* UNIT, VOLSER where received files are allocated    (system's choice)
* KEEPDAYS     days a finished transfer (delivered, confirmed,
*              rejected, failed) stays in the spool after its last
*              change; older ones are deleted once a day, data sets
*              never. 0 keeps them for ever                    (7)
* RELAY        Y: act as a node: take files for Odette IDs of our
*              partners (direct or VIA) and pass them on unchanged,
*              their EERP/NERP back to the sender               (N)
* SVC          the SVC number the cross-memory transport takes at
*              start, 200-255, NO DEFAULT: without it there is no
*              transport, and OFTPD says so (OFTP038I). OFTPD's
*              number is 237, assigned once for the whole ecosystem
*              -- never scan for a free one, because two products
*              that each pick "a free one" take the same slot on the
*              same system. OFTPD checks at start that the entry
*              still holds the invalid-SVC routine and refuses it
*              otherwise; it gives the entry back at stop and in its
*              recovery exit.
*
*              The OFTP utility and the ISPF dialog reach OFTPD
*              through it; without it they find no OFTPD.
* ADMIN        a userid that may see and change every transfer and
*              CALL partners; one ADMIN= per userid, at most 8.
*              Anyone else sees and changes only the transfers they
*              queued. Received files belong to nobody, so only an
*              ADMIN= userid sees them.                        (none)
*
* ADMIN=IBMUSER
*
ODETTEID=O0000000000MYMVS
PORT=3305 SVC=237
INPREFIX=OFTP.IN TMPPREFIX=OFTP.TMP
